so there was a social media summit at  the White House last week and over the  weekend I got so many messages from  people saying David you've got to talk  about it your boy Tim Poole was there it  was really this hilarious comedy of  errors it was punctuated most  hysterically actually by Twitter not  only not being invited to the social  media summit but Twitter's platform  actually went down during the summit and  became inaccessible so nobody could  tweet about what was going on is it was  happening for a whole bunch of the time  because Twitter was down I mean it's  seriously the stuff of legend but let's  actually break through let's break it  down piece by piece a little bit so  first of all the entire premise of the  summit was that Donald Trump believes  that conservative voices are being  targeted in silence by social media it's  not just Donald Trump who believed this  there's a huge contingent of the right  that believes that conservative voices  are being targeted and silenced by  Twitter by YouTube by Facebook they're  all left-wing as far as this conspiracy  theory goes and Donald Trump reportedly  told the room of people such innovative  and amazing insights as quote some of  you are extraordinary the crap you think  of is unbelievable and yet Facebook  wasn't invited  Google wasn't invited Twitter wasn't  invited but Donald Trump did say during  the summit that he would soon invite  them and that he would scold them in  person for the liberal bias that Donald  Trump believes that they exhibit so many  of the complaints from the right are  about the moderation of content but of  course the attendees to the summit  itself were required to submit their  questions in advance of the social media  summit if they wanted to say anything  independent journalist Tim Poole who  I've interviewed and know personally was  one of the invitees and he posted some  hilarious stuff from it including these  oversized boards with definitions for  words like shadow banning daxing D  platforming and D monetization which the  sign for D monetization describes is  preventing people from earning money for  their content based on political  viewpoints of platforms which of course  we have widely debunked the YouTube D  monetization that's going  and that is affecting us and the deep  prioritization of our content on YouTube  I have not seen any evidence that it's  politically biased and what if I thought  even remotely that that was the case I  would be saying  YouTube is de prioritizing and D  monetizing left-wing content like mine  but that would be dishonest I don't  believe that that's the case I don't  believe that what's going on is  politically biased it appears to be  biased against independent creators and  towards legacy establishment corporate  creators on the basis of just being safe  for big brands to advertise on so we've  talked about that already that's another  joke but then the funniest part again  was Twitter being down globally for  about an hour during the event so  there's some farcical elements here  there's the entire premise of the event  being conservatives are being widely  censored online and there's obvious  political bias against conservatives and  towards progressives online which is a  joke we are a great example of the  reality that that's not the case we've  talked about this many times before as  I've said previously just because a  company has sort of a center-left  culture or says hey you've got to use  the gender pronouns that people want to  be called by at work that doesn't mean  that the companies are inherently  left-wing in terms of their place and  the corporate status quo this would be  like saying that in 1962 a company that  had a policy that said we don't allow  calling black people the n-word oh  that's a liberally biased company that  it's ridiculous okay  number two the people selected for this  social media summit make the event truly  laughable I mean look at the list there  was a conspiracy theorist named Bill  Mitchell who promoted queuing on  conspiracy theories online that was  invited to the White House some guy  behind a pro Trump meme account on  Twitter that does nothing of actual  journalistic or socio political or  cultural commentary value Brent Bozell  who is one of the most storied  right-wing ideologues who once compared  Barack Obama to a skinny ghetto  crackhead he was invited as some kind of  media  project Veritas which completely flopped  where the bogus so-called investigation  into Planned Parenthood selling baby  parts was invited and then a smattering  of more established right-wing groups  I'm not mentioning everyone but I think  you sort of get the gist of it so to say  you want to figure out social media and  then you invite arranged of basically  whacked-out conservatives to centrists  it's terrible I told Tim Poole we were  chatting before the event and I said Tim  it would be really great if you showed  up and you said to Trump hey we really  should have had progressives here if you  can even by the way get yourself on  video mentioning you should have had  David Pakman here we would obviously  play that on the show that's just my  personal bias but in any case say  something about the total lack of  political diversity here other than  going basically from the center to the  extreme right I don't believe that that  happened but zoom out here a little bit  and you see the hilarious hypocrisy of  the event they hold an event to talk  about the supposed suppression of  conservative voices by social media they  invite no one that has actually being  been banned they suppress even  center-left  voices nevermind progressive ones and  they demand that everybody submit their  questions ahead of time effectively  putting in place the same type of  moderation that they criticize the right  won't even understand the absurdity of  this but this is sort of like the joke  that's no longer funny this is  weaponized ignorance as I've been saying  and it's inside the White House the  White House in this case is the source  of it rather than just the place that is  unable to deal what with what it is that  is going on out on social media and on  the Internet so I I couldn't tell you  one thing that was gained from doing  this other than seeing the just  hilarious  the hilariously inaccurate way in which  the White House claims to understand or  interpret what it is that's going out  there on social media
 

